<inputs>
Product Name: Ovel
Wordmark: "Ovel" in font Disolve (capital 'O', standalone text, never pair with logo icon side-by-side)
One-Line Promise: "One Ovelink for Everything You Book, Sell, or Schedule • 0% Commission"
Domain / Profile Handle: ovel.lk (customer links: ovel.lk/l/apex-studio, ovel.lk/l/lumina-skin)
Color Palette:
- Primary Brand Color: Deep Teal (#105F68)
- Canvas Background: Warm Porcelain Off-White (#F6FAF9)
- Secondary / Accents: Soft Sage (#3A9295), Mint Glow (#63C1BB), Light Seafoam (#C8E6E2, #9ED5D1)
- Data / Dark UI: Obsidian (#103438, #0D2629)
Typography:
- Wordmark: Disolve (capital 'O')
- Headlines / Display: Kaleko 105 or Disolve
- UI Data, Numerics & Tables: Geist or Inter (tight letter-spacing)
- URLs, Timestamps & Status Codes: Monospace (Geist Mono)
Key UI Moments (Ovel Platform):
1. The Ovelink Customer Profile (e.g. Apex Auto Lab or Lumina Skin Studio): 1-tap slot selection, service cards, automated buffer time indicator, instant deposit checkout.
2. The 3 Business Engines: Engine 01 (Appointments & Buffers), Engine 02 (Space & Station Rentals), Engine 03 (Custom Order Packages).
3. The Appointment & Order Roster (Merchant Dashboard): Station and specialist assignment (e.g. Dr. Genevieve Moreau • Station 02), Card-on-File status, and 1-click no-show fee enforcement.
4. Instant 2-Way WhatsApp Receipt & Calendar Sync.
5. The 0% Commission Metric: "LKR 0 Marketplace Cut" vs traditional 20% platform commission (LKR 3,600+/mo saved).
Real Merchant Footage:
- 10 to 16 vertical and landscape clips/photos across real business categories: precision vehicle detailing studio (Apex Auto Lab), medical aesthetics & skincare clinic (Lumina Skin), artisanal sourdough micro-bakery (Velvet Crumb), and creative podcast/photo loft.
Audio & SFX:
- Royalty-free track at 120 BPM with a clean buildup, impactful bass drop, and driving groove (e.g. Mixkit, free for commercial use).
- Tactile SFX library: mechanical keyboard keystrokes, soft UI pops, slot selection clicks, card deposit chime, and subtle camera shutter snaps.
</inputs>

<direction>
High-end minimal luxury. One idea per shot, lots of empty space, deep teal accent against warm porcelain canvas, one clean sans (Geist) with tight tracking. Masked type reveals, match cuts, one smooth camera language. Real footage only, never placeholder cards. No full stops in on-screen promotional text.

Strict Brand Rules:
- The wordmark must always be "Ovel" with a capital 'O' using font Disolve.
- Never place the logo icon and the "Ovel" text together side-by-side. If using text, do not include the icon; if using the icon, do not include text.
- Do not mention or show third-party consumer brands. Use neutral, device-agnostic terminology (e.g., "phone mockup", "desktop browser", "hardware frame", "status pill").
- Banned: Shockwave rings, particle bursts, RGB split, camera shake, lens flares, neon glows, grid floors, flashing backgrounds, bouncy easing.
</direction>

<structure>
10 bars at 120 BPM, 2 seconds each (20 seconds total). Every cut lands on a downbeat; every UI interaction hits on a beat.

Bar 1: The hook lands word by word on the beats through a sharp baseline mask onto the warm porcelain canvas (#F6FAF9):
"Stop" → "Paying" → "Twenty" → "Percent"
Heavy, crisp Geist typography in deep teal (#105F68).

Bar 2: The word "Percent" folds into an elegant pill input: "ovel.lk/l/apex-studio". A sleek dark cursor types and clicks "Create Ovelink". A deep teal circle expands rapidly from the button into a dark, sleek studio scene as the track builds to the peak.

The drop (Bar 3): Bass hits. The circle opens out of the button into a wall of real clips (detailing bay, aesthetic clinic, bakery oven, audio booth) with a scan line and 3 winners locking in the 3 Engines:
"01 Appointments" • "02 Space Rentals" • "03 Custom Orders"

Bar 4: The key output as big type: monumental type "0% TAKE-RATE" centered on screen, subtitle "Keep Every Cent You Earn" sliding from a mask, and a split comparison bar wiping across:
"Marketplace Cut: -LKR 3,600/mo" (draining in red) vs "Ovel Cut: LKR 0" (anchored in deep teal).

Bar 5: 3D carousel of real videos with floor reflections and a motion-blurred whip onto one hero clip: Apex Auto Lab's ceramic coating bay.

Bar 6: The hero in a phone mockup on the left with live slot selection ("10:00 AM – Signature Paint Correction LKR 450"), automated buffer calculation ("+30 Min Turnover Buffer"), and instant card deposit checkout.

Bar 7: A desktop panel flips into results on the right: the live "Appointment & Order Roster" populates with station assignment, active "Card on File" badge in soft mint (#63C1BB), and 1-click no-show protection ("Enforced ✓").

Bar 8: Big stats on push cuts:
"+LKR 3,561 KEPT MONTHLY" → "WHATSAPP 2-WAY RECEIPTS" → "100% DIRECT DEPOSITS"
Stacked into three clean horizontal badges.

Bar 9: 3-word kinetic ticker flashes in full-frame typography on downbeats:
"BOOK" → "SELL" → "SCHEDULE"
The canvas clears to pristine warm porcelain (#F6FAF9).

Bar 10: Ovel logo reveal: "Ovel" draws in cleanly in font Disolve (capital 'O', deep teal #105F68), tagline "One Link for Everything You Do" in Kaleko 105, domain badge "ovel.lk", and an elegant fade to black on the resolving kick.
</structure>

<build>
1. One HTML file at 1920x1080. Every style is computed from time inside window.seek(t): no CSS animations, no timers, no state between frames.
2. Real video: extract clips to 30fps JPEG sequences with ffmpeg (`ffmpeg -i clip.mp4 -q:v 2 frames/%04d.jpg`) and swap img sources per frame. seek awaits the image decodes.
3. Analyze the song with numpy: tempo (120 BPM), beat grid, energy per bar, the drop. Calibrate the grid to the real kick hits. Every cut sits on a downbeat, every UI hit on a beat.
4. Render with Playwright: 3 subframes per frame at t minus, at, and plus 1/240s, then blend with ffmpeg tmix for real motion blur at 60fps.
5. Place each sound effect so its measured peak, not its file start, lands on the event. Keep the effects quiet under the music. Loudnorm to -14 LUFS.
6. Probe 20 or more frames before the full render. Fix anything cluttered, overlapping or hard to read.
</build>

<gotchas>
Never set opacity or filter on a preserve-3d element, because it flattens and both faces show. Fade its wrapper instead. Measure element positions at runtime for match cuts. Pre-load and await all web fonts (Disolve, Kaleko 105, Geist) via document.fonts.ready before the first seek call. Keep "Ovel" in font Disolve with a capital 'O'. Never render a logo icon alongside the wordmark text. Device-agnostic presentation only; no third-party consumer brand references. Only use music and sound effects whose license allows commercial use (Mixkit).
</gotchas>

<start>
Ask me for the inputs, then show me a storyboard with every timing on the beat grid before you write any code.
</start>